  "term": "peripheral",
  "definition": "In this context, peripheral means located in the sensory organs outside the central nervous system rather than in brainstem or other central structures. The article uses it to describe changes in the vestibular organs themselves, including effects on the side of injury and temporary adaptation on the opposite side.",
